# sha256 of every version of every test file HITL has ever synced into a product repo.
#
# dev-update deletes a stale synced test ONLY when the file is tracked in the repo AND its content
# hashes to one of these. Name alone is not evidence of authorship: a team writing tests for the
# shipped validator `check_skips.py` will name theirs `test_check_skips.py` by pytest convention,
# and deleting that would destroy their work with no recovery path when it is untracked.
#
# A tracked file whose name matches but whose hash does not is reported, never deleted — it is
# either a team's own file or a HITL test they have edited. Both are theirs.
#
# Generated from the plugin repo's history; append a line when a synced test file changes or is
# retired. Format: <sha256>  <basename>
